    {
      "id": "scale",
      "type": "metrics",
      "duration_s": 7,
      "narration": [
        "Habitat is the storage layer OpenAI's products read from: over seventy million requests a second.",
        "It serves more than a billion people a week,",
        "and holds over five hundred petabytes.",
        "And it had to grow more than ten times a year, three years running."
      ],
      "data": {
        "cards": [
          {
            "label": "Requests per second",
            "value": "70M+",
            "compare": "almost 40 regions"
          },
          {
            "label": "People each week",
            "value": "1B+",
            "compare": "ChatGPT, API, Codex…"
          },
          {
            "label": "Data served",
            "value": "500 PB+",
            "compare": "one storage platform"
          }
        ],
        "footnote": "Growth: more than 10× year over year, for three years"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library",
      "type": "fanout",
      "duration_s": 10,
      "narration": [
        "Habitat started as a Python library, copied into every product that used it.",
        "Changing it meant rolling a new version out to dozens of services, which took days.",
        "Then one team rolled back to an old, buggy version, and caused the very outage they were preventing.",
        "So Habitat became one central service: one place to deploy, secure, and observe."
      ],
      "data": {
        "services": [
          "ChatGPT",
          "API",
          "Codex",
          "Sign-in",
          "Settings",
          "Billing",
          "Search",
          "Internal"
